1
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Once upon a time in Nazi occupied France...

2
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Inglourious Basterds is a drama, thriller, war
film directed by Quentin Tarantino.

3
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:03,000
In Nazi-occupied France during World War II, a group of Jewish-American soldiers known as "The Basterds" are
chosen specifically to spread fear throughout the Third Reich by scalping and brutally killing Nazis.

4
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:42,000
The Basterds, lead by Lt.

5
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Aldo Raine soon cross paths with a French-Jewish teenage girl who runs a
movie theater in Paris which is targeted by the soldiers.

6
00:45:54,000 --> 00:46:00,000
LT. Aldo Raine, played by Brad Pitt.

7
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:39,000
Shosanna, played by Mélanie Laurent.

8
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
COL. Hans Landa, played by Christoph Waltz.

9
01:08:51,000 --> 01:08:57,000
SGT. Donny Donowitz, played by Eli Roth.

10
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
LT. Archie Hicox, played by Michael Fassbender.

11
01:24:09,000 --> 01:24:15,000
Bridget von Hammersmark, played by Diane Kruger.

12
01:31:48,000 --> 01:31:54,000
Quentin Tarantino's Inglourious Basterds: Motion Picture Soundtrack is the
soundtrack to Quentin Tarantino's motion picture Inglourious Basterds.

13
01:39:27,000 --> 01:39:33,000
It was originally released on August 18, 2009.

14
01:47:06,000 --> 01:47:12,000
The soundtrack uses a variety of music genres, including Spaghetti Western soundtrack
excerpts, R&B and a David Bowie song from the 1982 remake of Cat People.

15
01:54:45,000 --> 01:54:51,000
"The Man with the Big Sombrero", a song from the 1943 screwball comedy Hi
Diddle Diddle, was rerecorded in French for the movie.

16
02:02:24,000 --> 02:02:30,000
This is the first soundtrack for a Quentin Tarantino
film not to feature dialogue excerpts.

17
02:10:03,000 --> 02:10:09,000
The album was nominated for a Grammy Award for Best Compilation Soundtrack Album for a Motion
Picture, Television or Other Visual Media, but lost to the Slumdog Millionaire soundtrack.

18
02:17:42,000 --> 02:17:48,000
The film explores themes of guerrilla warfare, paris, france,
self sacrifice, world war ii, jew persecution.

19
02:25:21,000 --> 02:25:27,000
The tone is intense and dark and emotional.
